00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.950 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  as you know the council is updating its  local plan  this is not a complete update of the  whole plan it is what is known as a  partial update  this means that we are updating certain  parts which includes topics that our  previous local plan inspectors  recommended  we are at quite an early stage of the  process so this video shares our  progress and provides information on a  consultation where you can have your say  please look at the documents and let us  have your comments by friday the 4th of  february 2022  don't forget this is only the start of  the local plan process  after we have gathered your views at  this stage of the process and compiled  further evidence we hope to publish a  draft plan in 2022  the draft plan will set out the detailed  policies and proposals for the area up  to 2040  there will be another chance for you to  comment before the draft plan is  finalized  as part of this partial update we have  published two key studies  the first is an update of the housing  needs assessment which identifies the  amount of housing the council needs to  allocate land for up to 2040  in line with government guidance and  provides more information about local  housing needs  the second is an update on the retail  and leisure study which indicates that  there is a little additional retail  floor space needed until 2040.  at this stage we have also published the  draft scoping report for the  sustainability appraisal of the local  plan  we have to assess the draft plan against  a range of social economic and  environmental criteria  and the draft scoping report proposes  what those criteria should be  this report has had comments from  natural england the environment agency  and historic england but we would like  to hear your comments on whether we have  identified the right criteria  we have also published two short  discussion papers on which we would  appreciate your views on these two  the first is about how we decide where  the focus of development should be  up to 2040.  in the adopted local plan the focus is  firstly on the towns and then the larger  villages  and the areas next to them and this was  agreed by the inspectors who looked at  the draft plan in 2019  the council needs to consider whether to  continue that focus or to look at  another option  the second is about the amount of jobs  we need to plan for up to 2040  kent county council have carried out  some work for us that suggests that we  need to plan for sites and buildings to  support around 11 000 jobs we would like  to hear people's views on the range and  number of jobs suggested  we have also reopened a call for sites  it is important that the sites the  council identifies to meet the local  development needs are suitable  available and deliverable  so it would be good to hear from agents  and landowners who believe they have  such sites which we can consider  if you would like to speak to one of the  local plan team before making comments  please get in touch  [Music]

